<title>ESTONIA: ESTONIA-LIVIKO PRIVATISATION PLAN APPROVED.</title>
<headline>ESTONIA-LIVIKO PRIVATISATION PLAN APPROVED.</headline>
<dateline>TALLINN 1997-07-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The government has approved the privatisation plan of Estonia's largest alcohol producer, Liviko, the government spokesman said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>He told Reuters that the plan had been approved at the evening sitting of the government.</p>
<p>Economy Minister Jaak Leimann had said that under the plan 44 percent of the company's shares will be privatised in a public offer this year.</p>
<p>Next year, 30 percent of its shares will be sold in an offer with preliminary negotiations and 21 percent in a public offer.</p>
<p>He had said the company should be sold by the end of next year.</p>
<p>The privatisation agency last year sold five percent of its shares, which are traded actively on the OTC market.</p>
<p>-- Eva Palu, Tallinn newsroom, +372 6209 201, reuters@reuters.ee</p>
</text>
